Next, determine how many trucks are required by dividing the total weight by the truck's capacity:

$$
\frac{6000 \text{ pounds}}{2000 \text{ pounds/truck}} = 3 \text{ trucks}
$$

Since the division results in a whole number, no additional trucks are needed for partial loads.

$$
\boxed{3}
